title: Harden forward-agent-log transcript export against secrets and record forgery
updated_at: "2026-07-15T05:20:33Z"
---
Implement a central outbound sanitisation boundary for forward-agent-log before formatting and delivery. Acceptance: strip NUL/C0/C1, ANSI/OSC, and bidi/spoofing controls; default-redact common secret-bearing material (authorization/bearer values, API-key shapes, JWTs, PEM private keys, credential assignments, URL userinfo/query secrets); frame every continuation line so transcript text cannot forge a new [user] or [agent] record; preserve UTF-8-safe max-bytes behaviour; add focused unit and binary fixture tests. Document that redaction is defence in depth and forwarded transcript text remains untrusted DATA.